    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "Although it is a music game, it does not require complicated controls or memorization of musical scores.<br />\r\nWhat is required is the ability to distinguish sounds.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe number of mines in a traditional minesweeper is represented by a number.<br />\r\nIn this game, the number of mines is represented by the sound of a piano.<br />\r\nIf there is one mine in the vicinity, one type of sound will be played.<br />\r\nIf there are three mines, three different sounds will sound simultaneously.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWhen you left-click, a sound is played if there are mines in the surrounding 8 squares.<br />\r\nIn addition, if the center square is unopened, it will be disclosed.<br />\r\nWith the right click, mines can be marked.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAnd each mine has a different phrase.<br />\r\nUnlike regular minesweepers, it is possible to identify not only the number of mines, but also the type of mine, so that<br />\r\nthere are very few cases where you are dependent on luck.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThere are also other elements that make the game more than just a minesweeper, such as squares where the sound cannot be confirmed after it has been disclosed.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n16 stages<br />\r\n8 pieces of classical music<br />\r\n4 arrangements of classical music<br />\r\n(The reason why the total number of songs does not add up to 16 is that there are overlapping stages.)",
    "about_the_game": "Although it is a music game, it does not require complicated controls or memorization of musical scores.<br />\r\nWhat is required is the ability to distinguish sounds.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe number of mines in a traditional minesweeper is represented by a number.<br />\r\nIn this game, the number of mines is represented by the sound of a piano.<br />\r\nIf there is one mine in the vicinity, one type of sound will be played.<br />\r\nIf there are three mines, three different sounds will sound simultaneously.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWhen you left-click, a sound is played if there are mines in the surrounding 8 squares.<br />\r\nIn addition, if the center square is unopened, it will be disclosed.<br />\r\nWith the right click, mines can be marked.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAnd each mine has a different phrase.<br />\r\nUnlike regular minesweepers, it is possible to identify not only the number of mines, but also the type of mine, so that<br />\r\nthere are very few cases where you are dependent on luck.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThere are also other elements that make the game more than just a minesweeper, such as squares where the sound cannot be confirmed after it has been disclosed.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n16 stages<br />\r\n8 pieces of classical music<br />\r\n4 arrangements of classical music<br />\r\n(The reason why the total number of songs does not add up to 16 is that there are overlapping stages.)",
    "short_description": "A new and innovative minesweeper that allows you to casually enjoy feeling like you have better ears. The number of mines in a traditional minesweeper is represented by a number. In this game, the number of mines is represented by the sound of a piano.",
